comments.body:
**R1-1** · nit · low · confirmed

**Known limits does not list every case that still ends up in the review body**

Decision 5 asks for the Known limits line to be narrowed to what remains. README.md:114 says the hunks come "from GitHub's whole-PR diff or, on a PR over 300 files, from the clone". The script asks the clone for any wanted file the whole diff gave no hunks for, whatever the PR's size (scripts/redline-gh.sh:353-357; shape.md deviation 20). The list of what stays in the body also leaves out four cases the code produces:
- a rename with no text changes, which has its own cause line (scripts/redline-gh.sh:437);
- a comment moved by the fallback after any other 422 (line 440);
- a path that git quotes in a diff header whatever the setting (a tab, a newline, a quote or a backslash), which neither source finds (recover_hunks header, lines 332-333; deviation 20);
- on a PR of 300 files or fewer, a file whose whole diff was refused or lacks it, when the clone lacks the commits.
Step 1 of docs/running.md (line 37) has a parenthetical of causes that leaves out the rename, "could not be had" and the fallback. That passage does point to "How the review is posted", which lists all of them except the quoted paths. Checked by reading the lines cited.

Proposed fix: Update the Known limits bullet in README.md (line 114). Say the clone is asked for any patch-less text file the whole diff does not give, on a PR of any size. Add to what stays in the body: a rename with no text changes, a comment the fallback moved after GitHub refused the review, a path git quotes in a diff header, and, on any PR, a patch-less file when the clone lacks the commits. In docs/running.md step 1, complete the parenthetical or mark it as examples.
